title:loadPhase
---
//when we declare new variable VSCode automatically designates a type, there's no need to hand-code a type.
<<declare $dialogPhase = "">>
<<declare $visitedYet = false>>
<<dialogPhaseSetter NPC>>
<<if $dialogPhase == "start">>
<<jump Start>>
<<elseif $dialogPhase == "quest_taken">>
<<jump quest_taken>>
<<elseif $dialogPhase == "quest_taken_return">>
<<jump quest_taken_return>>
<<elseif $dialogPhase == "repeat">>
<<jump repeat>>
<<elseif $dialogPhase == "repeat_return">>
<<jump repeat_return>>
<<elseif $dialogPhase == "quest_complete">>
<<jump quest_complete>>
<<elseif $dialogPhase == "quest_complete_return">>
<<jump quest_complete_return>>
<<else>>
NPC: I don't know what to do. This is an error debug message. Fix your shit.
<<endif>>
===

title: Start
---
<<set $visitedYet = true>>
<<cam_move NPC_Cam_Rig "npc">>
NPC: Hello there! I am Erling Haaland.
NPC: Welcome to the Erling Haaland and Jude Bellingham house.
NPC: Jude Bellingham is not here right now but that is okay.
NPC: I am in the middle of setting up for his gabber night of fun.
NPC: As a welcome back from his time playing for England.
NPC: While you're here, I actually have a favor to ask of you.
NPC: Can you help me?
<<cam_move NPC_Cam_Rig "pc">>
    ->I can help.
        <<dialogPhaseGetter NPC "quest_taken">>
        <<cam_move NPC_Cam_Rig "return">>
        <<jump quest_taken>>
    ->Not right now.
        <<dialogPhaseGetter NPC "repeat">>
        <<cam_move NPC_Cam_Rig "return">>
===

title: repeat
---
<<cam_move NPC_Cam_Rig "npc">>
NPC: Can you help me?
<<cam_move NPC_Cam_Rig "pc">>
    -> Sure.
        <<dialogPhaseGetter NPC "repeat">>
        <<cam_move NPC_Cam_Rig "return">>
        <<jump quest_taken>>
    -> Not right now.
        <<cam_move NPC_Cam_Rig "return">>
===

title: quest_taken
---
<<cam_move NPC_Cam_Rig "npc">>
NPC: Ah this is great!
NPC: I am hosting a huge night of gabber, as I said.
NPC: But I am missing Joost Klein.
NPC: I haven't heard from him and I am worried he got stuck somewhere.
NPC: I need you to go find him for me.
NPC: As I am stuck in this room and can't really leave like you can.
<<cam_move NPC_Cam_Rig "pc">>
    ->Sure.
        <<dialogPhaseGetter NPC "quest_taken_return">>
        <<cam_move NPC_Cam_Rig "return">>
    ->Not right now.
        <<dialogPhaseGetter NPC "repeat_return">>
        <<cam_move NPC_Cam_Rig "return">>
        <<jump repeat_return>>
===

title: repeat_return
---
<<cam_move NPC_Cam_Rig "npc">>
NPC: Can you please just find Joost for me dude ughhhh.
    -> Fine.
        <<dialogPhaseGetter NPC "quest_taken_return">>
        <<cam_move NPC_Cam_Rig "return">>
===

title: quest_taken_return
---
<<cam_move NPC_Cam_Rig "NPC">>
NPC: Welcome back my little chudling! Did you find Joost Klein?
<<cam_move NPC_Cam_Rig "pc">>
    -> Nope.
        <<cam_move NPC_Cam_Rig "return">>
===

title: quest_complete
---
<<cam_move NPC_Cam_Rig "npc">>
<<if $visitedYet == false>>
<<set $visitedYet to true>>
NPC: Joost Klein is that you!
NPC: I'm gonna take him off your hands.
NPC: Thank you stranger.
<<cam_move NPC_Cam_Rig "pc">>
    -> ...Okay.
        <<cam_move NPC_Cam_Rig "return">>
<<endif>>

<<if $visitedYet == true>>
<<cam_move NPC_Cam_Rig "npc">>
NPC: Joost Klein!
NPC: You have found him!
NPC: The gabber party is saved!
NPC: Jude Bellingham will be so happy
NPC: Thanks for bringing me the dutch guy.
NPC: You've saved the Jude Bellingham Welcome Home Gabber Party!
<<cam_move NPC_Cam_Rig "pc">>
    -> Love you king.
        <<cam_move NPC_Cam_Rig "return">>
<<dialogPhaseGetter NPC "quest_complete_return">>
<<endif>>
===

title: quest_complete_return
---
<<cam_move NPC_Cam_Rig "npc">>
NPC: You've saved the Jude Bellingham Welcome Home Gabber Party!
NPC: Thanks again friend.
<<cam_move NPC_Cam_Rig "return">>
===